From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:10:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] touch: the hold to calibrate after review

Follow-up to the previous patch (PR #91), after review:

- The hold no longer opens the overlay over the setup wizard: closing it
  hid the wizard's container (NavigationManager's go_back hides the
  screen's other children). In the full wizard it goes back to the
  wizard's own touch calibration step (force_touch_calibration_step,
  ui_wizard_navigate_to_step; leaving a running AD5X step aborts it, as
  Back does); in a targeted session (Settings > Printer > Run Setup
  Wizard, SETUP_WIZARD), which has no such step, it does nothing.
- Nothing fires while any calibration capture runs, the wizard's step
  too: the read callback checks CalibrationContext::capture_active and
  the handler DisplayManager::is_touch_calibration_active(), both set by
  every session's begin(). A press seen then does not fire after the
  calibration closes (the overlay's own hold-abort with the finger still
  down), only after 3 s with no touch.
- Open dialogs are closed first (ModalCloseReason::External, as the
  remote control's reset): push_overlay keeps modals above the new
  overlay, where they covered Accept and Retry. The reinstall offer
  (0088) takes that as a dismissal and asks again at the next start.
- The timing is TouchHoldGesture (touch_hold_gesture.h, no LVGL):
  releases under 70 ms (two readings at 33 ms) are noise, not 200 ms,
  which joined fast taps into a hold; a release seen and then a press
  after the gap starts a new press, also when no released reading came at
  the gap (a stale start time before); pressed readings far apart with no
  release between (a slow frame) stay one press. The finger must stay
  within 8% of the screen per axis of where the press began (driver
  points, before the affine): a scroll, a slider drag or a jog across
  the pad is no hold.
- On success the overlay path refreshes Settings > Touch & Input's
  status and clears /input/force_calibration, as the Settings and
  --calibrate-touch paths do (refresh_calibration_status() made public).
- A comment says why the widget gets PRESS_LOST twice.

What the hold opens is touch_hold_action(), also without LVGL. Tests in
test_kiln_touch_hold.cpp: the timing (10000 ms, once per press, the gap,
the re-arm, a stale press, fast taps, the radius, a stuck panel,
calibration on screen, the tick wrap), the choice of action, and the
path through calibrated_read_cb with a button (PRESS_LOST, no click,
wait_until_release, refused during a capture or by the handler).

Upstream: not applicable (Kiln OS specific)
